<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Notation and Cross-References</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout, <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>log</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the natural logarithm.
Key references: single capacity inequality equation <a href="#S3.E7" title="In Proposition 1 (Cascade Upper Bound via Data Processing). ‣ 3.2 Context-Conditional Capacities ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>; Fano–packing converse Thm. <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Fano–Packing Lower Bound (Bayes/Minimax Semantics)). ‣ 4.2 Fano–Packing Converse Lower Bound ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>; PAC–Bayes Thm. <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (PAC–Bayes for Observable Loss). ‣ 5.1 PAC–Bayes Bounds ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>; expected KL identity Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Expected KL Decomposition). ‣ 5.2 KL Decomposition and Capacity Control ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>; dataset information Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4 (From 𝒟 to (𝑈^𝑚,𝑆^𝑚,𝑌^𝑚)). ‣ 5.2 KL Decomposition and Capacity Control ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>; capacity-control Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Capacity Control of 𝐼(𝑈^𝑚,𝜃)). ‣ 5.2 KL Decomposition and Capacity Control ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>; Posterior Bayes–Loss Identity Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma7" title="Lemma 7 (Posterior Bayes–Loss Identity). ‣ Appendix I Posterior Bayes Loss Identity ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>; Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Loss–Index Link via a Measurable Partition). ‣ 4.1 Separable Codebooks and the Loss–Index Link ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Residual Information of the Algorithm). ‣ 5.3 Algorithmic Residual Information ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>; final statements in Sec. <a href="#S6" title="6 The Alignment Performance Interval ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Conditional Capacities and the Cascade</h2>

<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Cascade Upper Bound via Data Processing). ‣ 3.2 Context-Conditional Capacities ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The cascade <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\to H\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\to H\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> forms a Markov chain. The result follows directly from the data processing inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shannon, 1948</a>]</cite>, which states that for such a chain, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(U;Y\mid S=s)\leq I(U;H\mid S=s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(U;Y\mid S=s)\leq I(U;H\mid S=s)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(U;Y\mid S=s)\leq I(H;Y\mid S=s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(U;Y\mid S=s)\leq I(H;Y\mid S=s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking suprema over the respective families yields <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(U;Y\mid S=s)\leq C_{\mathrm{tot}\mid S}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>tot</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(U;Y\mid S=s)\leq C_{\mathrm{tot}\mid S}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. Averaging over <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> proves equation <a href="#S3.E7" title="In Proposition 1 (Cascade Upper Bound via Data Processing). ‣ 3.2 Context-Conditional Capacities ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Packing Constructions for Common Losses</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Binary Classification</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}=[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}=[M]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> the set of labels. Take <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{(i)}=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{(i)}=i</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math> and for any <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(u^{(j)},a^{(i)})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(u^{(j)},a^{(i)})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, giving <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> be the predicted label; Assump. <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Loss–Index Link via a Measurable Partition). ‣ 4.1 Separable Codebooks and the Loss–Index Link ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> holds with margin <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Pairwise Ranking with 0–1 Loss</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> encode a total order over items and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> be the fraction of misordered pairs. Use <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{(i)}=u^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{(i)}=u^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> (predict that order). Then <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math> and for any <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>, at least one pair flips, so <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\geq 1/{\binom{n}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\geq 1/{\binom{n}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>; with standard <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> pairwise loss averaged over all <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{n}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{n}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> pairs and normalized to <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimal separation is <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=1/{\binom{n}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=1/{\binom{n}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> output the predicted order; Assump. <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Loss–Index Link via a Measurable Partition). ‣ 4.1 Separable Codebooks and the Loss–Index Link ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> holds.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Truncated and Normalized MSE</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(u,a)=\min\{\|u-a\|^{2}/\tau^{2},1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(u,a)=\min\{\|u-a\|^{2}/\tau^{2},1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose an <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-separated packing <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> (under <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math>), and set <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{(i)}=u^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{(i)}=u^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math> and, for <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>, the prototype cross-loss satisfies <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(u^{(j)},a^{(i)})\geq r^{2}/\tau^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(u^{(j)},a^{(i)})\geq r^{2}/\tau^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
To make Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition6" title="Definition 6 (Δ-Separable Codebook). ‣ 4.1 Separable Codebooks and the Loss–Index Link ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Loss–Index Link via a Measurable Partition). ‣ 4.1 Separable Codebooks and the Loss–Index Link ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> hold with a single margin, take the common choice</p>
<table id="A3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\ =\ \frac{r^{2}}{4\tau^{2}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\ =\ \frac{r^{2}}{4\tau^{2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Indeed, for any <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> misclassified by the nearest-prototype Voronoi rule, one has <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|a-u^{(i)}\|\geq r/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|a-u^{(i)}\|\geq r/2</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(u^{(i)},a)\geq r^{2}/(4\tau^{2})=\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(u^{(i)},a)\geq r^{2}/(4\tau^{2})=\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2}/\tau^{2}\geq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2}/\tau^{2}\geq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the prototype cross-loss condition in Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition6" title="Definition 6 (Δ-Separable Codebook). ‣ 4.1 Separable Codebooks and the Loss–Index Link ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> also holds.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Fano–Packing Converse Details</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We expand the proof of Thm. <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Fano–Packing Lower Bound (Bayes/Minimax Semantics)). ‣ 4.2 Fano–Packing Converse Lower Bound ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Let <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> be uniform on <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[M]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=U^{(J)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=U^{(J)}</annotation></semantics></math>. With <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{J}=\phi(\pi(Y,S),S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{J}=\phi(\pi(Y,S),S)</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Risk ⇒ Index Error). ‣ 4.2 Fano–Packing Converse Lower Bound ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> gives <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R(\pi)\geq(\varepsilon+\Delta)\,\mathbb{P}\{\hat{J}\neq J\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\pi)\geq(\varepsilon+\Delta)\,\mathbb{P}\{\hat{J}\neq J\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The standard form of Fano’s inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shannon, 1948</a>]</cite>, when conditioned on <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, implies that
<math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(J\mid Y,S)\leq\mathbb{P}\{\hat{J}\neq J\}\log(M-1)+h_{2}(\mathbb{P}\{\hat{J}\neq J\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>J</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(J\mid Y,S)\leq\mathbb{P}\{\hat{J}\neq J\}\log(M-1)+h_{2}(\mathbb{P}\{\hat{J}\neq J\})</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives the more convenient bound</p>
<table id="A4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\{\hat{J}\neq J\}\ \geq\ 1-\frac{I(J;Y\mid S)+\log 2}{\log M}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>J</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\{\hat{J}\neq J\}\ \geq\ 1-\frac{I(J;Y\mid S)+\log 2}{\log M}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\to U\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\to U\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Information Reduction: 𝐽→𝑈→𝑌). ‣ 4.2 Fano–Packing Converse Lower Bound ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), we get equation <a href="#S4.E13" title="In Theorem 1 (Fano–Packing Lower Bound (Bayes/Minimax Semantics)). ‣ 4.2 Fano–Packing Converse Lower Bound ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>; then apply equation <a href="#S3.E7" title="In Proposition 1 (Cascade Upper Bound via Data Processing). ‣ 3.2 Context-Conditional Capacities ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> for equation <a href="#S4.E14" title="In Theorem 1 (Fano–Packing Lower Bound (Bayes/Minimax Semantics)). ‣ 4.2 Fano–Packing Converse Lower Bound ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>PAC–Bayes Details and Residual Control</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Proofs of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Expected KL Decomposition). ‣ 5.2 KL Decomposition and Capacity Control ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4 (From 𝒟 to (𝑈^𝑚,𝑆^𝑚,𝑌^𝑚)). ‣ 5.2 KL Decomposition and Capacity Control ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Expected KL Decomposition). ‣ 5.2 KL Decomposition and Capacity Control ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The identity is a foundational result in information-theoretic learning theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu and Raginsky, 2017</a>, <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Russo and Zou, 2019</a>]</cite>. The proof is as follows:
with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> independent of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}[\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D},\theta\sim P}\big[\log\tfrac{P(\theta\mid\mathcal{D})}{Q(\theta)}\big]=I(\mathcal{D};\theta)+\mathrm{KL}(p(\theta)\|Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}[\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D},\theta\sim P}\big[\log\tfrac{P(\theta\mid\mathcal{D})}{Q(\theta)}\big]=I(\mathcal{D};\theta)+\mathrm{KL}(p(\theta)\|Q)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4 (From 𝒟 to (𝑈^𝑚,𝑆^𝑚,𝑌^𝑚)). ‣ 5.2 KL Decomposition and Capacity Control ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Data processing gives <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(U^{m};\theta)\leq I(U^{m};\mathcal{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(U^{m};\theta)\leq I(U^{m};\mathcal{D})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(U^{m};Y^{m},S^{m})=I(U^{m};S^{m})+I(U^{m};Y^{m}\mid S^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(U^{m};Y^{m},S^{m})=I(U^{m};S^{m})+I(U^{m};Y^{m}\mid S^{m})</annotation></semantics></math>,
with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(U^{m};S^{m})=\sum_{i}I(U_{i};S_{i})=mI(U;S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(U^{m};S^{m})=\sum_{i}I(U_{i};S_{i})=mI(U;S)</annotation></semantics></math> by i.i.d.
For the conditional term, under the i.i.d. source and the memoryless channel <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y_{i}\mid u_{i},s_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y_{i}\mid u_{i},s_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(u^{m}\mid s^{m})=\prod_{i}p(u_{i}\mid s_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(u^{m}\mid s^{m})=\prod_{i}p(u_{i}\mid s_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and hence
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y^{m}\mid s^{m})=\prod_{i}\!\int p(y_{i}\mid u_{i},s_{i})\,p(u_{i}\mid s_{i})\,du_{i}=\prod_{i}p(y_{i}\mid s_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y^{m}\mid s^{m})=\prod_{i}\!\int p(y_{i}\mid u_{i},s_{i})\,p(u_{i}\mid s_{i})\,du_{i}=\prod_{i}p(y_{i}\mid s_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(Y^{m}\mid S^{m})=\sum_{i}H(Y_{i}\mid S_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(Y^{m}\mid S^{m})=\sum_{i}H(Y_{i}\mid S_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(Y^{m}\mid U^{m},S^{m})=\sum_{i}H(Y_{i}\mid U_{i},S_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(Y^{m}\mid U^{m},S^{m})=\sum_{i}H(Y_{i}\mid U_{i},S_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(U^{m};Y^{m}\mid S^{m})=\sum_{i}I(U_{i};Y_{i}\mid S_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(U^{m};Y^{m}\mid S^{m})=\sum_{i}I(U_{i};Y_{i}\mid S_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Controlling the Residual Term</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We list standard mechanisms to enforce Assump. <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Residual Information of the Algorithm). ‣ 5.3 Algorithmic Residual Information ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. These methods all serve to regularize the information that the learned parameters <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> contain about the specific training dataset <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<em id="A5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Algorithmic noise</em>: inject Gaussian noise into updates or use high-temperature posteriors; <em id="A5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">early stopping</em>: bound the mutual information by limiting the number of optimization steps; <em id="A5.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">posterior smoothing</em>: mix the learned posterior with the prior.
The general goal of controlling information flow, often framed as a form of compression, is a central theme in understanding deep learning generalization, although its precise role and benefits are still actively debated <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kawaguchi et al., 2023</a>, <a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Saxe et al., 2019</a>, <a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shwartz-Ziv et al., 2024</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2025</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>From Expectation to High Probability</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides a simple method to convert our expectation-based capacity bound on the KL-divergence into a high-probability statement. This type of conversion from expectation to high-probability bounds is a common step in applying learning-theoretic results. More sophisticated techniques can yield tighter, anytime-valid bounds that hold uniformly over time <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rodríguez-Gálvez et al., 2024</a>]</cite>. A direct application of Markov’s inequality suffices.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Markov Lift for the KL Term)<span id="Thmlemma5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X\triangleq\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≜</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\triangleq\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> denote the (dataset-dependent) PAC–Bayes KL term.
For any <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\eta</annotation></semantics></math> (over the draw of <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>),</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\ \leq\ \frac{\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}[X]}{\eta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\ \leq\ \frac{\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}[X]}{\eta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}[X]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}[X]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> under the conditions of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (PAC–Bayes for Observable Loss). ‣ 5.1 PAC–Bayes Bounds ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, Markov’s inequality gives</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left\{\,X&gt;\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}[X]}{\eta}\,\right\}\ \leq\ \eta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">{</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.500em">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left\{\,X&gt;\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}[X]}{\eta}\,\right\}\ \leq\ \eta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Equivalently, with probability at least <math id="A6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\eta</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\leq\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}[X]/\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\leq\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}[X]/\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, as claimed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(A Capacity-Aware High-Probability Upper Bound)<span id="Thmcorollary3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmcorollary3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\eta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\eta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. With probability at least <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta-\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta-\eta</annotation></semantics></math> (over the draw of <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>), the PAC–Bayes bound of Thm. <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (PAC–Bayes for Observable Loss). ‣ 5.1 PAC–Bayes Bounds ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> implies</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\theta\sim P}\big[R_{\mathrm{obs}}(\theta)\big]\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}_{\theta\sim P}\big[\widehat{R}^{\mathrm{obs}}_{m}(\theta)\big]\ +\ \sqrt{\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}[\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)]/\eta+\log(1/\delta)}{2m}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>obs</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi><mi>obs</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\theta\sim P}\big[R_{\mathrm{obs}}(\theta)\big]\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}_{\theta\sim P}\big[\widehat{R}^{\mathrm{obs}}_{m}(\theta)\big]\ +\ \sqrt{\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}[\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)]/\eta+\log(1/\delta)}{2m}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmcorollary3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Combining with Cor. <a href="#Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 1 (A Capacity-Aware Upper Bound). ‣ 5.3 Algorithmic Residual Information ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and applying a union bound yields, with the same probability,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\theta\sim P}\big[R_{\mathrm{obs}}(\theta)\big]\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}_{\theta\sim P}\big[\widehat{R}^{\mathrm{obs}}_{m}(\theta)\big]\ \ +\ \sqrt{\frac{m\,\bar{C}_{\mathrm{tot}\mid S}+m\,I(U;S)+\rho+\mathrm{KL}(p(\theta)\|Q)}{2m\,\eta}\ +\ \frac{\log(1/\delta)}{2m}}\ ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>obs</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi><mi>obs</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>tot</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\theta\sim P}\big[R_{\mathrm{obs}}(\theta)\big]\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}_{\theta\sim P}\big[\widehat{R}^{\mathrm{obs}}_{m}(\theta)\big]\ \ +\ \sqrt{\frac{m\,\bar{C}_{\mathrm{tot}\mid S}+m\,I(U;S)+\rho+\mathrm{KL}(p(\theta)\|Q)}{2m\,\eta}\ +\ \frac{\log(1/\delta)}{2m}}\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmcorollary3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><em id="Thmcorollary3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph">All constants are explicit; the price of eliminating the dataset randomness in <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)</annotation></semantics></math> is the slack parameter <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="Thmcorollary3.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Loss Truncation and Normalization</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For unbounded losses such as MSE, define <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(u,a)=\min\{\|u-a\|^{2}/\tau^{2},1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(u,a)=\min\{\|u-a\|^{2}/\tau^{2},1\}</annotation></semantics></math> for a scale <math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (report <math id="A7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> when plotting).
All PAC–Bayes statements and Thm. <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Fano–Packing Lower Bound (Bayes/Minimax Semantics)). ‣ 4.2 Fano–Packing Converse Lower Bound ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> require only <math id="A7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>; truncation ensures this and keeps statements coordinate-free.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Loss–Observable Link and Risk Transfer</h2>

<div id="Thmassumption4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 4</span></span><span id="Thmassumption4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Loss–Observable Link)<span id="Thmassumption4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmassumption4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist constants <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all measurable actions <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y,s)</annotation></semantics></math> in the support of <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,S)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A8.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\big[\ell(U,a)\,\big|\,Y=y,\,S=s\big]\ \leq\ \alpha\,\tilde{\ell}(y,s,a)\ +\ \beta\ ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi>α</mi><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.500em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\big[\ell(U,a)\,\big|\,Y=y,\,S=s\big]\ \leq\ \alpha\,\tilde{\ell}(y,s,a)\ +\ \beta\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span><span id="Thmlemma6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Risk Transfer)<span id="Thmlemma6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4 (Loss–Observable Link). ‣ Appendix H Loss–Observable Link and Risk Transfer ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, for any (possibly randomized) decoder <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A8.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[\ell\big(U,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S)\big)\big]\ \leq\ \alpha\,\mathbb{E}\big[\tilde{\ell}\big(Y,S,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S)\big)\big]\ +\ \beta\ ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[\ell\big(U,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S)\big)\big]\ \leq\ \alpha\,\mathbb{E}\big[\tilde{\ell}\big(Y,S,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S)\big)\big]\ +\ \beta\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, when <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn from the same codebook-induced mixture distribution used in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Fano–Packing Lower Bound (Bayes/Minimax Semantics)). ‣ 4.2 Fano–Packing Converse Lower Bound ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, taking <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\theta\sim P(\cdot\mid\mathcal{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\sim P(\cdot\mid\mathcal{D})</annotation></semantics></math> and expectation over both <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and the data gives</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\theta\sim P}\big[R_{\mathrm{mix}}(\pi_{\theta})\big]\ \leq\ \alpha\,\mathbb{E}_{\theta\sim P}\big[R_{\mathrm{obs}}(\theta)\big]\ +\ \beta\ ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>mix</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>obs</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\theta\sim P}\big[R_{\mathrm{mix}}(\pi_{\theta})\big]\ \leq\ \alpha\,\mathbb{E}_{\theta\sim P}\big[R_{\mathrm{obs}}(\theta)\big]\ +\ \beta\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the tower property and equation <a href="#A8.E26" title="In Assumption 4 (Loss–Observable Link). ‣ Appendix H Loss–Observable Link and Risk Transfer ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[\ell\big(U,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S)\big)\big]=\mathbb{E}\Big[\,\mathbb{E}\!\big[\ell(U,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))\mid Y,S\big]\,\Big]\leq\alpha\,\mathbb{E}\big[\tilde{\ell}(Y,S,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))\big]+\beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[\ell\big(U,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S)\big)\big]=\mathbb{E}\Big[\,\mathbb{E}\!\big[\ell(U,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))\mid Y,S\big]\,\Big]\leq\alpha\,\mathbb{E}\big[\tilde{\ell}(Y,S,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))\big]+\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Averaging over <math id="A8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\sim P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\sim P</annotation></semantics></math> yields the stated forms.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Posterior Bayes Loss Identity</h2>

<div id="Thmlemma7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7</span></span><span id="Thmlemma7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Posterior Bayes–Loss Identity)<span id="Thmlemma7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix any bounded loss <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and define
<math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\ell}^{\star}(y,s,a)\triangleq\mathbb{E}[\ell(U,a)\mid Y=y,\ S=s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\ell}^{\star}(y,s,a)\triangleq\mathbb{E}[\ell(U,a)\mid Y=y,\ S=s]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for any (possibly randomized) decoder <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and any data distribution over <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,S,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,S,Y)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[\tilde{\ell}^{\star}(Y,S,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))\big]\ =\ \mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[\tilde{\ell}^{\star}(Y,S,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))\big]\ =\ \mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the tower property of conditional expectation,
<math id="A9.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\tilde{\ell}^{\star}(Y,S,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))]=\mathbb{E}\{\mathbb{E}[\ell(U,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))\mid Y,S]\}=\mathbb{E}[\ell(U,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\tilde{\ell}^{\star}(Y,S,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))]=\mathbb{E}\{\mathbb{E}[\ell(U,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))\mid Y,S]\}=\mathbb{E}[\ell(U,\pi_{\theta}(Y,S))]</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix J </span>Residual Control via Posterior Compression</h2>

<div id="A10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A10.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\theta\sim P(\cdot\mid\mathcal{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\sim P(\cdot\mid\mathcal{D})</annotation></semantics></math> be the (possibly randomized) learner parameter.
Let <math id="A10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> be an auxiliary random seed, independent of <math id="A10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U^{m},S^{m},Y^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U^{m},S^{m},Y^{m})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider a data-independent randomized quantizer <math id="A10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> that maps <math id="A10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="A10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\theta}=T(\theta,W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\theta}=T(\theta,W)</annotation></semantics></math> taking at most <math id="A10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> distinct values.
Let <math id="A10.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> be the pushforwards of <math id="A10.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> through <math id="A10.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8</span></span><span id="Thmlemma8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Residual control by compression)<span id="Thmlemma8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathcal{D};\tilde{\theta}\mid U^{m})\ \leq\ H(\tilde{\theta})\ \leq\ \log K." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathcal{D};\tilde{\theta}\mid U^{m})\ \leq\ H(\tilde{\theta})\ \leq\ \log K.</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmlemma8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A10.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathcal{D};\tilde{\theta}\mid U^{m})\leq H(\tilde{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathcal{D};\tilde{\theta}\mid U^{m})\leq H(\tilde{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A10.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">, and <math id="A10.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\tilde{\theta})\leq\log K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\tilde{\theta})\leq\log K</annotation></semantics></math> since
<math id="A10.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> takes at most <math id="A10.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> values.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 9</span></span><span id="Thmlemma9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(KL does not increase under post-processing)<span id="Thmlemma9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmlemma9.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(P_{c}\|Q_{c})\ \leq\ \mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(P_{c}\|Q_{c})\ \leq\ \mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmlemma9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A10.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{c},Q_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{c},Q_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (PAC–Bayes for Observable Loss). ‣ 5.1 PAC–Bayes Bounds ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Expected KL Decomposition). ‣ 5.2 KL Decomposition and Capacity Control ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> yields the
capacity-aware bound of Corollary <a href="#Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 1 (A Capacity-Aware Upper Bound). ‣ 5.3 Algorithmic Residual Information ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with <math id="A10.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\leq\log K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\leq\log K</annotation></semantics></math>. This approach is conceptually related to other works that leverage model compression or selection of small representative subsets to derive non-vacuous generalization bounds for overparameterized models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Leblanc et al., 2025</a>, <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lotfi et al., 2024</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A11" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix K </span>Context Coarsening</h2>

<div id="A11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}=T(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}=T(S)</annotation></semantics></math> for a measurable (data-release) channel <math id="A11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\to S\to S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\to S\to S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> forms a Markov chain (that is, <math id="A11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated from <math id="A11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> without direct access to <math id="A11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>).
Then by data processing <math id="A11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(U;S^{\prime})\leq I(U;S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(U;S^{\prime})\leq I(U;S)</annotation></semantics></math>.
All definitions and bounds in the paper hold verbatim with <math id="A11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in place of <math id="A11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>,
with capacities recomputed as <math id="A11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{C}_{\mathrm{tot}\mid S^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>tot</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{C}_{\mathrm{tot}\mid S^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and dataset information term
<math id="A11.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\,I(U;S^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\,I(U;S^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> replacing <math id="A11.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\,I(U;S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\,I(U;S)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, for any preprocessor <math id="A11.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, Corollary <a href="#Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 1 (A Capacity-Aware Upper Bound). ‣ 5.3 Algorithmic Residual Information ‣ 5 PAC–Bayes Upper Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> becomes</p>
<table id="A11.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A11.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}\!\big[\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)\big]\ \leq\ m\,\bar{C}_{\mathrm{tot}\mid S^{\prime}}\ +\ m\,I(U;S^{\prime})\ +\ \rho\ +\ \mathrm{KL}(p(\theta)\|Q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>tot</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}\!\big[\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)\big]\ \leq\ m\,\bar{C}_{\mathrm{tot}\mid S^{\prime}}\ +\ m\,I(U;S^{\prime})\ +\ \rho\ +\ \mathrm{KL}(p(\theta)\|Q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A11.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Choosing <math id="A11.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> to enforce <math id="A11.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(U;S^{\prime})\leq\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(U;S^{\prime})\leq\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> makes the interference term <math id="A11.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\,\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\,\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> explicit.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A12" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix L </span>Soft Loss–Index Link</h2>

<div id="A12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume there exists a measurable <math id="A12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathcal{A}\times\mathcal{S}\to[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathcal{A}\times\mathcal{S}\to[M]</annotation></semantics></math> and parameters
<math id="A12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon,\Delta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon,\Delta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="A12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="A12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A12.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\big\{\,\mathbb{E}[\ell(U^{(i)},a)\mid S]\ \geq\ \varepsilon+\Delta\ \big|\ \phi(a,S)\neq i\,\big\}\ \geq\ 1-\zeta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\big\{\,\mathbb{E}[\ell(U^{(i)},a)\mid S]\ \geq\ \varepsilon+\Delta\ \big|\ \phi(a,S)\neq i\,\big\}\ \geq\ 1-\zeta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then for any decoder <math id="A12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A12.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{J}=\phi(\pi(Y,S),S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{J}=\phi(\pi(Y,S),S)</annotation></semantics></math>, writing <math id="A12.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E\!\triangleq\!\{\hat{J}\neq J\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≜</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\!\triangleq\!\{\hat{J}\neq J\}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A12.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="G\!\triangleq\!\big\{\mathbb{E}[\ell(U^{(J)},\pi(Y,S))\mid S]\geq\varepsilon+\Delta\big\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≜</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\!\triangleq\!\big\{\mathbb{E}[\ell(U^{(J)},\pi(Y,S))\mid S]\geq\varepsilon+\Delta\big\},</annotation></semantics></math>
we have</p>
<table id="A12.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U,\pi(Y,S))\big]\ =\ \mathbb{E}\!\Big[\,\mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U^{(J)},\pi(Y,S))\mid S\big]\cdot\mathbf{1}_{E}\Big]\ +\ \mathbb{E}\!\Big[\,\mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U^{(J)},\pi(Y,S))\mid S\big]\cdot\mathbf{1}_{E^{c}}\Big]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U,\pi(Y,S))\big]\ =\ \mathbb{E}\!\Big[\,\mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U^{(J)},\pi(Y,S))\mid S\big]\cdot\mathbf{1}_{E}\Big]\ +\ \mathbb{E}\!\Big[\,\mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U^{(J)},\pi(Y,S))\mid S\big]\cdot\mathbf{1}_{E^{c}}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A12.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq\ (\varepsilon+\Delta)\,\mathbb{P}(E\cap G)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq\ (\varepsilon+\Delta)\,\mathbb{P}(E\cap G),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.p1.3" class="ltx_p">hence</p>
<table id="A12.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U,\pi(Y,S))\big]\ \geq\ (\varepsilon+\Delta)\,\mathbb{P}(E)\ -\ (\varepsilon+\Delta)\,\mathbb{P}(E\cap G^{c})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U,\pi(Y,S))\big]\ \geq\ (\varepsilon+\Delta)\,\mathbb{P}(E)\ -\ (\varepsilon+\Delta)\,\mathbb{P}(E\cap G^{c}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.p1.4" class="ltx_p">By the assumption, <math id="A12.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(G^{c}\mid E)\leq\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(G^{c}\mid E)\leq\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A12.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(E\cap G^{c})\leq\zeta\,\mathbb{P}(E)\leq\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(E\cap G^{c})\leq\zeta\,\mathbb{P}(E)\leq\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> and consequently</p>
<table id="A12.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U,\pi(Y,S))\big]\ \geq\ (\varepsilon+\Delta)\,\mathbb{P}\{\hat{J}\neq J\}\ -\ \zeta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>J</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U,\pi(Y,S))\big]\ \geq\ (\varepsilon+\Delta)\,\mathbb{P}\{\hat{J}\neq J\}\ -\ \zeta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.p1.5" class="ltx_p">A slightly tighter but equivalent multiplicative form also holds:</p>
<table id="A12.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U,\pi(Y,S))\big]\ \geq\ (\varepsilon+\Delta)\,(1-\zeta)\,\mathbb{P}\{\hat{J}\neq J\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[\ell(U,\pi(Y,S))\big]\ \geq\ (\varepsilon+\Delta)\,(1-\zeta)\,\mathbb{P}\{\hat{J}\neq J\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Consequently, Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Fano–Packing Lower Bound (Bayes/Minimax Semantics)). ‣ 4.2 Fano–Packing Converse Lower Bound ‣ 4 Information-Theoretic Lower Bounds ‣ The Alignment Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> holds with an additive <math id="A12.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> (or multiplicative <math id="A12.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\\
zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\\
zeta)</annotation></semantics></math>) slack in the lower bound.</p>
</div>
</section>
